    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "healing feels like such a joke though. like what am i supposed to heal back into? the version of me that actually mattered is gone. i look in the mirror and i don't even recognize the person staring back. it's just... empty. there's no spark left, no reason to even keep maintaining this body when the soul of it has already left.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings of emptiness and questioning whether healing is worth it are incredibly valid when the part of you you thought mattered feels lost. However, the person you see in the mirror today isn't necessarily a replacement for who you were, but rather a new vessel capable of holding different kinds of strength that you haven't discovered yet. Sometimes renaming this journey as \"adaptation\" instead of \"healing\" can feel less like losing something and more like making space for a different, unexpected version of yourself to emerge.",
      "source": "target",
